### All requests go through the Ocelot API Gateway
@gateway = http://localhost:5000

### 1. Create a student  -> publishes StudentCreatedIntegrationEvent
POST {{gateway}}/api/students
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Asha",
  "lastName": "Patel",
  "email": "asha.patel@uni.edu",
  "dateOfBirth": "2002-05-14",
  "phoneNumber": "9876543210"
}

### 2. Create a course  -> publishes CourseCreatedIntegrationEvent
POST {{gateway}}/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "CS501",
  "title": "Distributed Systems",
  "description": "Microservices, messaging and eventual consistency",
  "instructor": "Dr. Rao",
  "credits": 4,
  "capacity": 30,
  "startDate": "2026-11-01"
}

### 3. See what Enrollment service received via RabbitMQ (its local read models)
GET {{gateway}}/api/enrollments/read-models/students

###
GET {{gateway}}/api/enrollments/read-models/courses

### 4. Enroll  -> publishes StudentEnrolledIntegrationEvent
POST {{gateway}}/api/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": 1,
  "courseId": 1
}

### 5. Gateway aggregate: student + their enrollments in one call
GET {{gateway}}/api/dashboard/students/1

### 6. Notifications generated from events
GET {{gateway}}/api/notifications

###
GET {{gateway}}/api/notifications/recipient/asha.patel@uni.edu

### 7. Cancel an enrollment  -> publishes EnrollmentCancelledIntegrationEvent
POST {{gateway}}/api/enrollments/1/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Schedule conflict"
}

### 8. Delete a student -> StudentDeleted -> Enrollment cancels active enrollments -> EnrollmentCancelled -> Notification
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/students/1
